<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The account type as the contacts apps read it. EditSchema lists the fields the phone's contacts app offers
    when it creates or edits a Mémento contact: the name and the phone numbers only (the rest is entered in
    Mémento; rows of other kinds that the files put on the phone are still shown, and kept, by the contacts app).

    The rules, from AOSP packages/apps/Contacts (Samsung Contacts is derived from it):
    https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/apps/Contacts/+/refs/heads/main/src/com/android/contacts/model/account/ExternalAccountType.java
    https://android.googlesource.com/platform/packages/apps/Contacts/+/refs/heads/main/src/com/android/contacts/model/account/BaseAccountType.java
    - areContactsWritable() is "has a valid EditSchema". Without one, or when the EditSchema breaks a rule
      (DefinitionException), the type falls back to the name and the photo, read-only: the very symptom seen on
      Samsung (a name-only editor, then a contact that cannot be edited at all), which the schema of 9f964b3
      produced (supportsPrefix="false"). A broken rule rejects the whole type, so the schema keeps only kinds
      DAVx5 also declares, and ContactsRegressionTest.accountTypeFollowsTheAospRules checks the rules below.
    - "name" (maxOccurs="1") must have supportsPrefix, supportsMiddleName, supportsSuffix and the three
      supportsPhonetic* all true ("For now, every thing must be supported").
    - "photo" is mandatory (checkKindExists(Photo.CONTENT_ITEM_TYPE)) with maxOccurs="1": it cannot be left out.
      Mémento has no photos; one set on the phone stays on the phone (an update keeps it).
    - a kind with a type column ("phone") needs at least one Type, each a name known to its KindBuilder.
    Attribute set shaped like DAVx5's, whose writable address books Samsung Contacts edits:
    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bitfireAT/davx5-ose/main-ose/core/src/main/res/xml/contacts.xml
    (supportsFamilyName and supportsDisplayName are not read by AOSP; kept as DAVx5 has them.)

    The prefix and the middle name are read into the first name, the suffix into the last name; the phonetic
    name stays on the phone (an update writes it back) but is not copied into the files.

    inviteContactActivity / inviteContactActionLabel (no namespace, read by ExternalAccountType.inflate): on a
    contact of ANOTHER account the contacts app may offer "Ajouter à Mémento", which starts MainActivity with
    com.android.contacts.action.INVITE_CONTACT and the contact's lookup URI (an import, ContactRequestFlow).
-->
<ContactsAccountType
    inviteContactActivity="app.memento.MainActivity"
    inviteContactActionLabel="@string/invite_contact_label">
    <EditSchema>
        <DataKind
            kind="name"
            maxOccurs="1"
            supportsDisplayName="true"
            supportsFamilyName="true"
            supportsPrefix="true"
            supportsMiddleName="true"
            supportsSuffix="true"
            supportsPhoneticFamilyName="true"
            supportsPhoneticMiddleName="true"
            supportsPhoneticGivenName="true" />
        <DataKind kind="photo" maxOccurs="1" />
        <DataKind kind="phone">
            <Type type="mobile" />
            <Type type="home" />
            <Type type="work" />
            <Type type="other" />
            <Type type="custom" />
        </DataKind>
    </EditSchema>
</ContactsAccountType>
